      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Interesting middle ground between the way that pedestals used to work and how they do now. I like the idea of being able to locally choose to download and view the avatar in more detail before trying it on. As long as it doesn't go back to loading every avatar pedestal because we all know how performant that was. This could be handy for avatar creators testing in game too. \nAlternatively I may suggest switching to holo port locomotion which should allow some further viewing of the avatar as it walks around you.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-12T11:51:42.335Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Problem: \nWhenever I want to look through some avatars on my own, \nI go through alot of Avatar worlds. \nWhen I go into an Avatar there is usually only a picture of it, \nand a mirror that lets me look at myself.\n\nBut sometimes I'd love to look at the character in detail, \neven look from the behind. \nYes, I can look at the avatar preview in the Avatar selection screen, \nbut for me as an Oculus Rift CV1 user, \nit's way too small and spins very fast.\n\nSuggestion:\nI'd love to be able to put a t-posed model of the avatar right in front of me,\nin it's actual size,\nand be able to look at it from all angles.\nJust like deploying a portal in front of me,\nI could deploy the avatar I have currently selected in the avatar select screen.",
